27864deb [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 569B 7.25s
27864deb [gemini-3.8-flash] #To set up the Blackmagic Design Intensity Pro 4K on Arch Linux, you will need the proprietary
27864deb [gemini-3.8-flash] #Blackmagic Desktop Video drivers, which are maintained by the community in the Arch User Repository
27864deb [gemini-3.8-flash] #(AUR).
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #Here is an overview of the steps required to get the card operational:
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Install Kernel Headers
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #The Blackmagic driver compiles a Dynamic Kernel Module Support (DKMS) module. You must have the
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #kernel headers installed for your active kernel before building the package:
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• For the default kernel: `linux-headers`
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• For the LTS kernel: `linux-lts-headers`
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• For any hardened or zen variants, choose the corresponding `-headers` package.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Install the Desktop Video Driver
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #The necessary drivers and utilities are packaged in the AUR under the name `desktopvideo`.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #You can build and install this using your preferred AUR helper (such as `paru` or `yay`) or by
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #cloning the repository from the AUR and building it manually with `makepkg`.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #Optional packages in the AUR you may also find useful:
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `desktopvideo-gui`: Provides the Blackmagic Desktop Video Setup utility for adjusting
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #card inputs, outputs, and format settings via a graphical interface.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `media-express`: The official capture and playback application provided by Blackmagic
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #Design.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Enable the Background Service
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #The hardware relies on a helper daemon to communicate with software. After installing the package:
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Enable and start the `DesktopVideoHelper.service` using `systemctl`.
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #4. Check Firmware Status
27864dec [gemini-3.8-flash] #The Intensity Pro 4K often requires a firmware check or update after driver updates:
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Run the `BlackmagicFirmwareUpdater status` command to ensure the on-board firmware matches the
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #installed driver version.
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #• If an update is required, the utility will prompt you to apply it and reboot the machine.
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #5. Verify the Kernel Modules
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #Ensure the `blackmagic` and `blackmagic-io` modules load successfully. You can verify this using
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #`lsmod`.
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #Once the service is active and the firmware is verified, the card should be immediately accessible
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #to applications such as OBS Studio, DaVinci Resolve, or FFmpeg.
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #Please let me know if you would like specific command examples, assistance configuring the DKMS
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #modules, or guidance for a particular capture application.
27864ded [gemini-3.8-flash] #
