279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Here is an outline and architecture for a generic tree-node data structure and multi-column
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #renderer suitable for directory listings and hierarchical views:
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. The Generic Tree Node Structure
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Using an interface with generic metadata allows the same tree-traversal and column-formatting logic
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #to be reused across file directories, ASTs, share listings, or menu structures.
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #interface TreeNode<T = Record<string, unknown>> {
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	name: string;
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	path: string;
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	isLeaf: boolean;
279df9e8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	children?: TreeNode<T>[];
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	metadata?: T;
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #}
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Architecture & Pipeline
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Breaking the implementation into discrete, named functions keeps each responsibility isolated:
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Hierarchy Builder (`buildDirectoryTree`):
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Reads directories asynchronously up to a designated depth.
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Partitions entries into folders (branches) and files (leaves).
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Sorts nodes systematically (e.g., branches first, then alphabetical).
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Tree Flattening / Traversal (`flattenTree`):
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Walks the tree (depth-first or breadth-first) to produce an ordered flat list.
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Attaches indent prefixes (such as standard box-drawing glyphs `├── `, `└── `, `│   `) or
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #produces composite path tokens depending on whether a tree-graph or a flat column layout is
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #desired.
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Column Formatter (`renderColumns`):
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Queries terminal width (`Deno.consoleSize().columns` or fallback).
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Computes the maximum visible character width of all rendered node labels (accounting for wide
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #unicode/emoji widths using `stringWidth`).
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Calculates the optimal column count and row count.
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * Formats the items into rows using vertical (down-first) column-major ordering.
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Tree-Graph Representation vs. Multi-Column Mode
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #A generic node tree structure allows switching between two distinct presentation modes based on
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #command arguments:
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9e9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Indented Hierarchy (Traditional Tree):
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #  Useful when recursing through nested directories (`/dir /r 3`).
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Dense Column Grid (Multi-Column Leaf Listing):
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #  Useful for flat views of current directories, organizing leaf names and folder tags across
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #balanced horizontal columns without line overflowing.
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #Would you like the full TypeScript implementation containing these named functions formatted with
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #tabs for `relay.ts`?
279df9ea [gemini-3.8-flash] #
