279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #Here is how and where it is typically applied:
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Research and Dataset Repositories
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #• CRediT Taxonomy: In academic and research repositories (e.g., Zenodo, Figshare, Dryad),
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #contributor roles often follow the CRediT (Contributor Roles Taxonomy) standard. One of the
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #14 official roles is "Data Curation", which encompasses managing, annotating, cleaning, and
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #maintaining research data.
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Citation File Format (`CITATION.cff`): When preparing citation metadata for repositories
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #containing data or software, curation roles are frequently specified in author and contributor
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #metadata.
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Hugging Face / Machine Learning: Repositories hosting datasets, model collections, or
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #benchmarks routinely credit contributors as "Data Curators" or "Dataset Curators".
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Open-Source Resource Lists ("Awesome" Lists)
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Repositories that aggregate tools, libraries, or articles (such as GitHub "Awesome" lists) often
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #credit maintainers and major contributors as "Curators" or note "Curated by
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #[Name]", rather than traditional software engineering titles like "Developer" or "Author".
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Open-Source Contributor Frameworks
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #• All Contributors Specification: While the default emoji key uses categories like `data`
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #or `content`, projects frequently adapt these definitions to credit curation work explicitly in
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #`README.md` contributor tables.
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #Phrasing Recommendation
279eedde [gemini-3.8-flash] #For clarity and consistency with standard contributor conventions, noun or participle forms are
279eeddf [gemini-3.8-flash] #generally preferred over the base verb:
