28489510 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.004 14.18KB 13.95s
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #I decoded the GDScript and cross-read it against the ClassDB reference. Here's my commentary.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #• What `scrape.gd` does*
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #A headless `SceneTree` bootstrap (`_init` → export → `quit`) that walks `ClassDB.get_class_list()`,
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #buckets every class into `node` / `resource` / `object` / `editor`, collects Variant type names,
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #and writes a tab-indented JSON "engine schema" (`res://godot_api_schema.json`) carrying package
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #metadata for the `nitrologic/biblispec` repo.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #• New / different vs. the ClassDB doc*
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #- The doc is stock Godot `ClassDB` API reference — nothing custom.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #- The script's categorization logic is the only non-standard part, and it maps cleanly onto
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #documented methods, so it's consistent with the reference.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #• Issues worth fixing*
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #1. `print_err(...)` in the failure branch of `export_engine_schema` is not a Godot function. There
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #is no such global; the correct calls are `printerr()` (stderr print) or `push_error()`. Because
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #GDScript resolves globals at compile time, this is a hard parse/compile error, so the script will
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #fail to load entirely — not just on the error path. This is the most important finding.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #2. The `object` bucket is effectively the full class list. Every engine class ultimately inherits
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #`Object`, so `ClassDB.is_parent_class(current_name, "Object")` is true for all of them. That's
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #presumably intentional as a catch-all, but it means `object` duplicates `ClassDB.get_class_list()`
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #and is not a meaningful partition alongside `node`/`resource`.
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #3. `is_editor_class` uses a name-prefix heuristic (`"Editor"`, `"ResourceImporter"`). The reference
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #exposes a purpose-built alternative: `ClassDB.class_get_api_type()` returning `API_EDITOR` /
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #`API_EDITOR_EXTENSION`. That would also catch editor extension classes the prefix test
28489511 [deepseek-flash] #misses, and avoid false positives on non-editor classes that merely start with "Editor".
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #4. `get_variant_names` starts at `range(1, TYPE_MAX)`, skipping `TYPE_NIL` (0). `"Variant"` is
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #prepended manually and the `names.has()` guard dedupes it when the loop reaches `TYPE_VARIANT`, so
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #no duplicate — but "Nil" is silently dropped. Worth deciding deliberately.
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #5. `ClassDB.get_class_list()` returns all classes regardless of enablement. If the schema should
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #reflect a runnable build, `ClassDB.is_class_enabled()` is available to filter.
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #• Minor*
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #- Sorting each bucket after population is fine and deterministic.
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #- Version string assembly and the metadata block look correct; no `Engine.get_version_info()` key
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #issues.
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #If you want, I can sketch a corrected `export_engine_schema` using `class_get_api_type` and
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #`printerr` — say the word and I'll post it.
28489512 [deepseek-flash] #
