2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #Notes worth knowing:
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #- Rebindable alternative. Add an action (`toggle_fullscreen`) in Project Settings → Input
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #Map, bind F12 to it, then test `event.is_action_pressed("toggle_fullscreen")` instead of the raw
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #keycode. Cleaner if you ever expose rebinding.
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #- `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` vs `EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN`. The former is borderless fullscreen
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #(better for alt-tab and multi-monitor); the latter grabs the display exclusively. If you only want
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #the borderless kind, drop the exclusive entry from the check.
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #- macOS caveat. F12 is bound to Dashboard/Mission Control by default at the OS level, so
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #the key may never reach the window unless the user disables that shortcut. Many laptops also
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #require holding Fn.
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #- Window focus. The key only arrives if the game window has focus; when running from the
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #editor the running window, not the editor, must be focused.
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #- `set_input_as_handled()` prevents the event from also reaching `_input`/UI nodes.
2848a815 [deepseek-flash] #
