2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #One clarification on why it matters, in case that's the underlying question: `_unhandled_input`
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #runs after `_input` and after the UI/`Control` nodes have had their chance, so by the time
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #your handler sees the event it's already "unclaimed." Marking it handled stops it from being passed
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #on to anything listening later in the same frame (other `_unhandled_input` handlers,
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #`_unhandled_key_input`), and keeps a keypress from also being consumed by the viewport's own
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #shortcuts. If you never mark it, the toggle still works — you just risk double-processing if more
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #than one node watches F12.
2848acbf [deepseek-flash] #
