2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.001 25.43KB 4.35s
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #Yes — a header comment is the usual way, since Godot ignores it and it costs nothing at runtime.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #Something like:
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] ## Style: one call per statement — no inline call chains (e.g. get_viewport().foo()).
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] ##        Prefer named helpers over inlining logic.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] ##        Single-statement guards may sit on the `if` line; else-branches may not.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] ##        Tabs for indentation.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #A few things to weigh:
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #- Keep it to the rules that aren't obvious. "Tabs" and "no inline calls" earn their place
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #because a reader can't infer them from the code below. "Use meaningful names" doesn't.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #- Header comments repeat. If every file carries the same block, edits mean touching every
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #file. A single `STYLE.md` (or `CONTRIBUTING.md`) at the repo root is the more standard home, and
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #each file can just point at it: `# Style: see STYLE.md`.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #- If the goal is enforcement, not documentation, a comment won't do it — `gdformat` /
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #`gdlint` (the gdtoolkit package) or an `.editorconfig` will actually hold the line and catch
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #violations. A comment only helps a human who reads it.
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #
2848b44e [deepseek-flash] #Which are you after — a note for human readers, or something you want tooling to enforce? If it's
2848b44f [deepseek-flash] #the former, tell me the exact rules you want stated and I'll tighten the wording.
2848b44f [deepseek-flash] #
