28b25227 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.004 554B 6.06s
28b25227 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In AWS web-based terminals (such as AWS CloudShell or EC2 Instance Connect), there is no desktop
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #"About" or application menu bar because the shell runs inside your web browser.
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Depending on the terminal tool being used, colors can be adjusted through the following methods:
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. AWS CloudShell (Built-in Web Settings)
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If using AWS CloudShell:
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Look at the top-right corner of the CloudShell pane (near the minimize/close buttons).
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Click the gear icon (Settings).
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• In the settings menu, there are options to adjust:
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #  * Theme (Light vs. Dark)
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #  * Font size
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. EC2 Instance Connect
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #EC2 Instance Connect's browser console does not provide a graphic settings menu for terminal
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #themes. To adjust colors there:
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Shell Prompt (`PS1`) and Highlights: Color changes must be made directly within your
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #shell configuration file (such as `~/.bashrc` or `~/.bash_profile`) using standard ANSI escape
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #codes.
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Directory Listing Colors: You can configure `LS_COLORS` or use `dircolors` to customize
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #file and folder color schemes.
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Browser Extension / Contrast: Browser-level high-contrast or dark-mode extensions will
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #also invert or restyle the canvas/terminal output.
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Alternative: Use a Local Terminal Client
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #For complete control over color schemes, palettes, and fonts:
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Connect to your EC2 instances or AWS environment using your local operating system's terminal
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #(e.g., iTerm2, Windows Terminal, Alacritty, GNOME Terminal) via SSH or the AWS Systems Manager
28b25228 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Session Manager plugin (`aws ssm start-session`).
28b25229 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Local terminal emulators provide full GUI preferences for palettes, background colors, and
28b25229 [gemini-3.8-flash] #transparency.
28b25229 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
