28b372dc [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Permissions (`drwx---rwx` / `707`)
28b372dc [gemini-3.8-flash] #Most of the directories (`aerialgrid`, `hd-aerialgrid`, `roagrid`, `topogrid`) have `drwx---rwx`
28b372dc [gemini-3.8-flash] #permissions:
28b372dc [gemini-3.8-flash] #• User (`http`): `rwx` (read, write, execute)
28b372dc [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Group (`http`): `---` (no permissions)
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Others (world): `rwx` (read, write, execute)
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #This is unusual because the group has zero access while any user on the system has full write
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #access. Usually, for a web server like Apache or Nginx running under the `http` user, you would
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #want directories set to `755` (`rwxr-xr-x`) like `sd-aerialgrid`, or group-shared permissions like
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #`775` (`rwxrwxr-x`) with your user added to the `http` group.
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b372dd [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Timestamps (`Jan 18 2026`)
