28b37d81 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Fast, Clean Copy for Many Small Files
28b37d81 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d81 [gemini-3.8-flash] #For millions or thousands of small files, `rsync` with the following flags is the safest and most
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #efficient tool. It preserves permissions, ownership, timestamps, and symlinks while avoiding
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #bottlenecks:
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #sudo rsync -aHAX --info=progress2 /srv/http/grid/ /mnt/grid26/
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Flag breakdown:*
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `-a` (archive): Recursively copies and preserves permissions, timestamps, owners, groups, and
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #symlinks.
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `-H`: Preserves hard links.
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `-A`: Preserves ACLs (access control lists).
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `-X`: Preserves extended attributes.
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `--info=progress2`: Gives a real-time aggregate transfer speed and overall percentage rather than
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #printing millions of individual filenames to the console (which slows down the transfer
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #significantly).
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	Note on the trailing slashes:*
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #	sing `/srv/http/grid/` (with a trailing slash) places the subdirectories directly inside
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`/mnt/grid26/` (e.g., `/mnt/grid26/aerialgrid`).
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. "Soft Mounting" (Bind Mount vs. Symlink)
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In Linux, there are two standard ways to map `/srv/http/grid` to `/mnt/grid26`:
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d82 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Option A: Bind Mount (Recommended for Web Servers)
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #A bind mount makes `/mnt/grid26` appear directly at `/srv/http/grid` at the filesystem level. Web
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #servers (Nginx, Apache, Caddy) handle bind mounts transparently without needing special settings
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #for symlink following or security restrictions.
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Once the transfer completes and you are satisfied:
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   # Move old data out of the way or back it up
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   sudo mv /srv/http/grid /srv/http/grid.bak
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   sudo mkdir -p /srv/http/grid
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Test the bind mount:
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   sudo mount --bind /mnt/grid26 /srv/http/grid
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Make it permanent in `/etc/fstab` (append to the end of the file):
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   /mnt/grid26    /srv/http/grid    none    bind    0    0
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Option B: Symlink (Soft Link)
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you prefer a traditional symbolic link:
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Move or remove the original folder:
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d83 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   sudo mv /srv/http/grid /srv/http/grid.bak
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Create the link:
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   sudo ln -s /mnt/grid26 /srv/http/grid
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• (Note: If using a symlink, ensure your web server configuration allows following symlinks, e.g.,
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`Options FollowSymLinks` in Apache or proper root handling in Nginx).*
28b37d84 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b37d84 [roha] *Note on the trailing slashes:**
28b37d84 [roha] sing `/srv/http/grid/` (with a trailing slash) places the subdirectories directly inside `/mnt/grid26/` (e.g., `/mnt/grid26/aerialgrid`).
