28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #The current context contains the `biblispec` specification document (version 1.5.9). Below is an
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #inventory of its primary sections and datasets:
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Root Metadata
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `name`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `symbol`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `version`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `description`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `status`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `copyright`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `license`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `repository`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `motto`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `separator`
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Specification Modules (`spec`)
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `numbers` / `counts` / `digits`: Numbering systems, numeric glyph
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #variants, and multi-script digit sets.
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `ASCII` / `ANSI`: Control character mnemonics, ANSI escape sequences, function
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #key modifiers.
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `symbols` / `shortcode` / `fenced` / `faces`: Curated symbol
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #sets, shortcodes, glyph sets, box-drawing characters, and visual profiles.
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `pheme`: Scientific, taxonomic, and linguistic prefixes and suffixes.
28b6c6f2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `scales`: Western music scales, intervals, degrees, and solfège.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `glagolitic` / `linear_b` / `phoenician` / `hebrew` /
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`coptic` / `greek` / `latin` / `reo`: Alphabets, syllabaries,
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #ideograms, and linguistic lexicons.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `unicode`: Selected Unicode blocks, mathematical alphanumeric variations, hieroglyphs,
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Braille, and alchemical notations.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `encoding`: FourCC RIFF tag definitions.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `relay`: Cuneiform / Akkadian structural language relay definitions.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `technology`: Solid-state LED/laser history and Windows Virtual-Key code lists.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `geography`: UN-recognized nations, ambiguous territories, and historical/defunct states.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `food`: Regional flatbreads and pancake taxonomies.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `internet`: Submarine optical cable installations and cloud availability zone coordinates
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #(AWS, Alibaba Cloud).
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `systemic fails`: Descriptions of non-linear failure cascades.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `fundament` / `orient`: Core ontological archetypes and spatial/conceptual
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #reference points.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `identifier`: Regular expressions and specifications for academic and system identifiers.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `citation`: Field specifications for scholarly citation standards.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Schemas and Definitions
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `schema`: Structural specifications for relays and sub-objects.
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `types`: Type definitions (e.g., `PathItem`).
28b6c6f3 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
