28b6ca5d [gemini-3.8-flash] #Here is a curated set of double-struck (blackboard bold) symbols widely used across engineering
28b6ca5d [gemini-3.8-flash] #disciplines, applied physics, computer science, statistics, and discrete mathematics that would
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #complement the existing set in `biblispec`:
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #Computer Science and Digital Logic
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝔹`: The Boolean domain \0, 1\ or \\textfalse, \texttrue\; foundational in switching
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #theory, digital logic synthesis, and type systems.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝔻`: The set of dyadic rationals (m/2^n); standard in numerical analysis, fixed-point
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #digital arithmetic, and computer hardware precision specifications.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #Control Engineering and Signal Processing
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕂`: The base field of scalars (conventionally specifying either \mathbbR or \mathbbC);
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #used in linear systems analysis, state-space representations, and functional analysis.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕋`: The circle group or 1D torus (\mathbbR/\mathbbZ, the unit circle in the complex
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #plane); standard domain for the Discrete-Time Fourier Transform (DTFT) frequency response.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕏`: The state space or input domain in dynamical systems, optimal control (Kalman
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #filtering), and system identification.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕐`: The measurement or output observation space in sensor networks and state-estimation
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #frameworks.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕃`: The operational Laplace domain or Leech lattice; frequently encountered in
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #continuous-time filter designs and telecommunication sphere-packings.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #Statistics, Machine Learning, and Information Theory
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝔼`: The expectation (expected value) operator; universally applied in statistical
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #signal processing, stochastic control, and loss-function formulation.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕍`: The variance operator; used in measurement uncertainty quantification,
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #instrumentation calibration, and estimation theory.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕀`: The indicator function (evaluating to 1 when a condition holds, 0 otherwise);
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #alternatively used for the identity matrix/operator.
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝟙`: The vector of all ones, or the characteristic/indicator operator in optimization
28b6ca5e [gemini-3.8-flash] #and graph theory (e.g., adjacency and Laplacian matrices).
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #Physics, Mechanics, and Geometry
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝔸`: Affine space \mathbbA^n; preferred in kinematics, robotics, and computer vision
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #where geometric objects and coordinate frames exist independently of a privileged origin.
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕄`: Minkowski spacetime (\mathbbM^1,3 or \mathbbM⁴); standard in relativistic
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #electrodynamics, wave propagation, and theoretical physics.
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝔾`: The Grassmannian manifold \mathbbG(k, n); used in multi-camera computer vision,
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #subspace tracking, and robotic motion planning.
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #• `𝕎`: The space of Walsh functions (orthogonal sequences in CDMA and telecommunications)
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #or the Wiener process in stochastic differential systems.
28b6ca5f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
