28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Looking closely at the log excerpt, a few key details stand out:
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. The Manual Mount Succeeded
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #At `15:34:02`, your manual mount command ran without errors:
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Sep 18 15:34:02 archlinux sudo[10700]: COMMAND=/usr/bin/mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/grid26
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Sep 18 15:34:03 archlinux kernel: EXT4-fs (sda1): mounted filesystem 0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f r/w with ordered data mode.
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #This confirms that:
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• The filesystem is healthy (`ext4`).
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• The target directory `/mnt/grid26` exists.
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• The disk's filesystem UUID is: `0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f`.
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Why Nginx Threw Errors Earlier
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Around `15:18` to `15:22`, Nginx generated a long stream of `2: No such file or directory` errors
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #trying to read from `/srv/http/grid/...`. Because `/dev/sda1` had not yet been mounted to
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`/mnt/grid26`, the underlying files were unavailable to the web server.
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Why `fstab` Did Not Mount It at Boot
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #During the system boot sequence around `14:19:13`, systemd logged no mount attempt or failure
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #for `/mnt/grid26`.
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #When a mount fails due to a bad option or disk delay, systemd logs an explicit failure unit
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #(`mnt-grid26.mount: Mount process exited...`). The total absence of any log entry usually indicates
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #one of the following:
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. The entry in `/etc/fstab` has the `noauto` mount option, which instructs systemd to
28b7a980 [gemini-3.8-flash] #ignore the entry during boot.
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. There is a typo or syntax error in `/etc/fstab` that caused `systemd-fstab-generator` to
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #ignore or fail to parse the line.
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. The line does not exist or was commented out.
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Recommended Next Steps
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #To verify how the line is currently defined in `/etc/fstab`, run:
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #grep "grid26" /etc/fstab
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #For reliable, automatic mounting on Arch Linux, the standard configuration for this partition using
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #the UUID reported by the kernel would look like this:
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #UUID=0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f  /mnt/grid26  ext4  defaults  0  2
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• (Using the UUID instead of `/dev/sda1` prevents mount failures if the drive letters shift during
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #future boots.)*
28b7a981 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
