152)\nSep 18 15:30:31 archlinux kernel: amdgpu 0000:0c:00.0: [drm] *ERROR* Unsupported screen format RA24 little-endian (0x34324152)\nSep 18 15:30:31 archlinux kernel: amdgpu 0000:0c:00.0: [drm] *ERROR* Unsupported screen format RA24 little-endian (0x34324152)\nSep 18 15:30:31 archlinux kernel: amdgpu 0000:0c:00.0: [drm] *ERROR* Unsupported screen format RA24 little-endian (0x34324152)\nSep 18 15:32:03 archlinux flatpak[9389]: [2:54:0918/153203.429230:ERROR:google_apis/gcm/engine/registration_request.cc:291] Registration response error message: DEPRECATED_ENDPOINT\nSep 18 15:34:02 archlinux sudo[10700]:     skid : TTY=pts/1 ; PWD=/home/skid/nitrologic ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/grid26\nSep 18 15:34:02 archlinux sudo[10700]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session opened for user root(uid=0) by skid(uid=1000)\nSep 18 15:34:03 archlinux kernel: EXT4-fs (sda1): mounted filesystem 0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f r/w with ordered data mode. Quota mode: none.\nSep 18 15:34:03 archlinux sudo[10700]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session closed for user root\nSep 18 15:34:50 archlinux accounts-daemon[1588]: Unable to open /etc/tcb: No such file or directory\nSep 18 15:34:50 archlinux accounts-daemon[1588]: couldn't list homed users: GDBus.Error:org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NameHasNoOwner: Could not activate remote peer 'org.freedesktop.home1': activation request failed: unknown unit\nSep 18 15:36:41 archlinux sudo[10894]:     skid : TTY=pts/1 ; PWD=/mnt/grid26 ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/chown -R skid:skid hd-aerialgrid\nSep 18 15:36:41 archlinux sudo[10894]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session opened for user root(uid=0) by skid(uid=1000)\nSep 18 15:37:15 archlinux sudo[10894]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session closed for user root\nSep 18 15:37:31 archlinux sudo[10966]:     skid : TTY=pts/1 ; PWD=/mnt/grid26 ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/chown -R skid:skid sd-aerialgrid\nSep 18 15:37:31 archlinux sudo[10966]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session opened for user root(uid=0) by skid(uid=1000)\nSep 18 15:37:33 archlinux sudo[10966]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session closed for user root\nSep 18 15:37:57 archlinux sudo[11026]:     skid : TTY=pts/1 ; PWD=/mnt/grid26 ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/chown -R skid:skid aerialgrid\nSep 18 15:37:57 archlinux sudo[11026]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session opened for user root(uid=0) by skid(uid=1000)\nSep 18 15:39:36 archlinux sudo[11026]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session closed for user root\nSep 18 15:39:39 archlinux sudo[11105]:     skid : TTY=pts/1 ; PWD=/mnt/grid26 ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/chown -R skid:skid aerialgrid\nSep 18 15:39:39 archlinux sudo[11105]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session opened for user root(uid=0) by skid(uid=1000)\nSep 18 15:40:22 archlinux sudo[11105]: pam_unix(sudo:session): session closed for user root\nSep 18 15:40:57 archlinux accounts-daemon[1588]: Unable to open /etc/tcb: No such file or directory\nSep 18 15:40:57 archlinux accounts-daemon[1588]: couldn't list homed users: GDBus.Error:org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NameHasNoOwner: Could not activate remote peer 'org.freedesktop.home1': activation request failed: unknown unit\n","name":"content"},{"role":"user","content":"Files shared. Feel free to comment if content is new or different.","name":"friend"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Looking closely at the log excerpt, a few key details stand out:\n\n### 1. The Manual Mount Succeeded\nAt `15:34:02`, your manual mount command ran without errors:\n```text\nSep 18 15:34:02 archlinux sudo[10700]: COMMAND=/usr/bin/mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/grid26\nSep 18 15:34:03 archlinux kernel: EXT4-fs (sda1): mounted filesystem 0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f r/w with ordered data mode.\n```\nThis confirms that:\n* The filesystem is healthy (`ext4`).\n* The target directory `/mnt/grid26` exists.\n* The disk's filesystem UUID is: `0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f`.\n\n### 2. Why Nginx Threw Errors Earlier\nAround `15:18` to `15:22`, Nginx generated a long stream of `2: No such file or directory` errors trying to read from `/srv/http/grid/...`. Because `/dev/sda1` had not yet been mounted to `/mnt/grid26`, the underlying files were unavailable to the web server.\n\n### 3. Why `fstab` Did Not Mount It at Boot\nDuring the system boot sequence around `14:19:13`, **systemd logged no mount attempt or failure for `/mnt/grid26`**. \n\nWhen a mount fails due to a bad option or disk delay, systemd logs an explicit failure unit (`mnt-grid26.mount: Mount process exited...`). The total absence of any log entry usually indicates one of the following:\n\n1. **The entry in `/etc/fstab` has the `noauto` mount option**, which instructs systemd to ignore the entry during boot.\n2. **There is a typo or syntax error** in `/etc/fstab` that caused `systemd-fstab-generator` to ignore or fail to parse the line.\n3. **The line does not exist** or was commented out.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nTo verify how the line is currently defined in `/etc/fstab`, run:\n\n```bash\ngrep \"grid26\" /etc/fstab\n```\n\nFor reliable, automatic mounting on Arch Linux, the standard configuration for this partition using the UUID reported by the kernel would look like this:\n\n```text\nUUID=0e219626-8fc2-4789-b3f7-fc5e3f0ef07f  /mnt/grid26  ext4  defaults  0  2\n```\n\n*(Using the UUID instead of `/dev/sda1` prevents mount failures if the drive letters shift during future boots.)*"},{"role":"user","content":"thanks!","name":"friend"},{"role":"assistant","content":"You are very welcome! If you need any assistance updating your `/etc/fstab` or adjusting permissions later on, feel free to ask. Have a great day!"},{"role":"system","content":"models under test include kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"user","content":"hi kimi all good?","name":"friend"}]}
