28ba9b72 [kimi-k2.7-code] #The wiki for this project is currently the `dsptool.md` file in `web/`. A few things I noticed:
28ba9b72 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba9b72 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Content: It’s a Markdown document with a table of contents and short summaries for each
28ba9b72 [kimi-k2.7-code] #DSP component (sensor, log, meter, keys, synth, system, display, floor, gamepad, acid32, files,
28ba9b72 [kimi-k2.7-code] #pico, lights, serial, navigator).
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Serving: In `http.h`, `.md` files are loaded and run through `markUp()` with the registry
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #map, so the server can substitute `${...}` variables before sending them.
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Integration: `dsplab.html` has a `<div section id="wiki"></div>` where the frontend
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #presumably loads `dsptool.md`, but the actual `dspwiki.js` renderer wasn’t included in this share.
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Notes: `web/notes.txt` looks like a scratchpad with extra snippets (emoji table, CSS
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #fragments, wiki `<div>` markup) that may be intended for the wiki or the UI.
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #What would you like me to do with the wiki — review/expand the content, wire up the frontend
28ba9b73 [kimi-k2.7-code] #renderer, or something else?
