28bac712 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Globals:* `wiki`, `wikiDiv`, `wikiTools`, `wikiHome`, `wikiRefresh`, `wikiAddress`,
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #`wikiEdit`, `wikiDebug`, `wikiPreview`, `wikiSave`, `wikiEmoji`, `WikiAnchors`, `homeWiki`,
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #`goWiki`, `onWikiGet`, `onWikiWrite`, `onWikiAddress`, `onWikiEdit`, `onWikiDebug`,
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #`onWikiPreview`, `onWikiSave`, `onWikiRun`, `onWikiEmoji`.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Sturdiness:* Core read/save/preview loop is solid and simple — plain string keys in Redis
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #make it easy to inspect and back up externally. However, several rough edges remain: the emoji
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #picker's data fetch (`nitrojs/json/emoji.json`) is commented out, so the panel currently renders
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #empty; `back()` navigation is non-functional (`this.history` is never populated, and the method
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #reads the global browser `history` object rather than the instance field); `run()` is a placeholder
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #stub that scans lines for a leading digit but performs no execution; and `WikiAnchors` (hash-based
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #navigation) is hardcoded `false`, so deep-linking via `#wiki.<key>` in `onHash()` (`dsptool.js`) is
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #currently the only working navigation path — the toolbar's `Home` button does not update the URL
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #hash. Currently only mounted on the Lab page (`dsplab.html`); other shells (Desktop, Studio,
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #Device, Map, Sandbox) omit the `#wiki` div entirely, so this instrument is Lab-only for now.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #A few things worth confirming/fixing before finalizing the doc, since they affect what "sturdy"
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #claims you can honestly make:
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Emoji fetch is dead code — either re-enable `getJSON("nitrojs/json/emoji.json",
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #this.refresh.bind(this))` in the `Wiki` constructor, or remove the emoji panel/button until it's
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #wired up.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. `back()` is broken — it references the free variable `history` (window.history) instead
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #of `this.history`, and nothing ever pushes onto `this.history`.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. No caller for `requestPage()` — this alternate direct-fetch path exists but `go()`
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #always uses the Redis RPC route instead; worth noting as dead/alternate code or removing.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #4. KaTeX dependency isn't declared in any of the `dsp*.html` script lists you shared, so
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #the `latex` fenced block feature would currently throw a `ReferenceError` at runtime if exercised.
28bac713 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bac714 [claude-sonnet-5] #Want me to also draft the Table of Contents line and index number update for `dsptool.md`,
28bac714 [claude-sonnet-5] #or go ahead and flag/fix the `back()` bug and the dead emoji fetch in `dspwiki.js`?
28bac714 [claude-sonnet-5] #
