28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.546 682.2KB 10.86s
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #On Arch Linux, the removal command depends on which "Sticky Notes" package you actually have
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #installed. Here's how to find and remove it:
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Find the package name
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #pacman -Qs sticky
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad475 [claude-sonnet-5] #or search more broadly:
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #pacman -Qs notes
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you installed it from the AUR (common ones: `sticky-notes`, `xpad`, `indicator-stickynotes`),
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #use `yay`/`paru` instead of `pacman` for querying — they share the same query flags.
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Common candidates and their removal commands
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If it's the Flatpak "Sticky Notes" (com.vixalien.sticky-notes) or similar GNOME extension
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #app:*
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak uninstall com.vixalien.sticky-notes
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If it's `xpad` (classic X11 sticky notes):*
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -Rns xpad
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If it's a GNOME Shell extension (e.g. "Sticky Notes" from extensions.gnome.org):*
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #gnome-extensions uninstall sticky-notes@blob.blob.gmail.com
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #(the exact UUID varies — check `gnome-extensions list`)
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If it's an AUR package:*
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad476 [claude-sonnet-5] #yay -Rns sticky-notes
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] ## or
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #paru -Rns sticky-notes
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. General uninstall pattern for pacman
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #Once you know the exact package name, `-Rns` removes the package, its dependencies not needed
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #elsewhere, and its config/cache files:
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -Rns <package-name>
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you tell me exactly how you installed it (pacman, AUR helper, Flatpak, Snap, GNOME extension, or
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #a manually built app), I can give you the precise command.
28bad477 [claude-sonnet-5] #
