28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.541 683.9KB 5.15s
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #Yes — the command is `flatpak list` (note: "flatpak", not "flatpack").
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak list
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #Useful variations:
28bad661 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak list --app          # only applications (hide runtimes)
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak list --app --columns=application,name,version
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak list | grep -i sticky   # search for sticky notes specifically
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you find the Sticky Notes entry, grab its Application ID column and uninstall with:
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak uninstall <application-id>
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #For example, if it shows up as `com.vixalien.sticky-notes`:
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #flatpak uninstall com.vixalien.sticky-notes
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #Run `flatpak list --app` first and let me know what you see if you want help identifying the right
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #entry.
28bad662 [claude-sonnet-5] #
