28bb29b4 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Objectives
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Validate that the JSON-RPC surface at `/api` cannot be abused to read/write arbitrary files,
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #execute arbitrary Redis commands, or spawn/control processes without authorization.
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm session/token handling cannot be predicted, replayed, or hijacked.
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm static file serving cannot be used for path traversal, information disclosure, or
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #resource exhaustion.
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Assess resilience of the connection-handling model (per-thread blocking I/O, sleep-based
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #throttling) to DoS.
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Identify hardcoded secrets, weak crypto usage, and transport-level exposure (plaintext HTTP).
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Scope
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #• In scope*
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `hostIPv4` / `hostIPv6` listeners on port 8083 (http.h)
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `/api` JSON-RPC dispatcher (`InvokeRPC`, `parseRPC` in headless.h)
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Static asset serving under `StaticPath` / `GridPath`
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Redis/Valkey backend as reached through the RPC layer (not direct network access, unless
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #explicitly authorized separately)
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Session/event polling mechanism (`sys.tick`, `sys.info`, `EventSink`)
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Process bridging (`sys.connect`, `sys.write`, `Process` class)
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Out of scope (unless separately authorized)*
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Direct network access to Redis/Valkey port 6379
28bb29b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #- ALSA/DRM/video/bluetooth native subsystems (not currently wired to `InvokeRPC`, but re-check at
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #test time)
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Physical/hardware access paths
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Methodology Phases
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 1 — Reconnaissance & Mapping
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Enumerate all reachable endpoints: `GET /`, static paths under `web/`, `/api` POST.
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Enumerate all RPC `method` values by diffing against `InvokeRPC` (`sys.info`, `sys.tick`,
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #`sys.refresh`, `sys.if`, `sys.rpc`, `sys.connections`, `sys.connect`, `sys.write`, `redis.run`,
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #`redis.process`, `redis.scan`, `redis.sub`, `redis.sink`, `redis.put`, `sys.shutdown`,
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #`sys.clocks`, `sys.setclock`, `sys.memory`, `sys.logs`, `sys.pcap`, `sys.ports`, `sys.open`,
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #`fs.folder`, `fs.file`).
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Fingerprint server via response headers, error text, timing (no `Server:` header suppression
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #observed — confirm).
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Identify whether TLS is terminated anywhere (reverse proxy) — the native listeners appear to be
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #plaintext HTTP only.
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 2 — Transport & Session Security
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm whether any RPC traffic — including `redis.put` file uploads and `sys.info` tokens —
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #traverses the network unencrypted. If no TLS-terminating proxy is present, treat this as a
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #finding, not a test artifact.
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Analyze session token generation: `connectSession()` computes
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #`sha512(("Connection"+ConnectionCount), ConnectSalt)`. Test:
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Predictability: since `ConnectionCount` is a small monotonically increasing integer and the
28bb29b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #salt is static/compiled-in, attempt to pre-compute/guess tokens for adjacent low session counts.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Replay: capture a valid `sessionName`/token pair from `sys.info` and confirm whether it can be
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #reused from a different origin/IP.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Fixation: verify `sessionMap` entries are never invalidated (no logout/expiry path is visible)
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #— test whether stale sessions remain valid indefinitely.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm `sys.tick` cannot be used to inject events (`postMessage`) into another session's queue
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #by guessing/brute-forcing `sessionkey`.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 3 — RPC Input Validation & Injection
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `redis.run` — this method passes the client-supplied `params->string` almost directly
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #into `redis.runRedis`/`RedisContext::run`, which itself parses quoted args and forwards to
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #`redisCommand`/`redisCommandArgv`. Treat this as effectively an unauthenticated Redis command
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #execution proxy unless something upstream restricts it. Test:
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - `FLUSHALL`, `CONFIG SET`, `EVAL` (Lua sandbox escape attempts), `SCRIPT LOAD`, `DEBUG`,
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #`SHUTDOWN`.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Command-injection via crafted quoting in the argument parser (`parseCommand`) — test unbalanced
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #quotes, embedded nulls, backslash edge cases.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Blind command chaining via `redis.process` (iterates an array of "commands" that are actually
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #treated as blob keys — confirm they can't be abused to enumerate/read arbitrary blob keys belonging
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #to other uploads).
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `redis.put` — uploads content, hashes it, stores as `blob.<hash>`, and records an
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #`upload.<hash>` hash-set entry with attacker-controlled `name`/`type`/`size` fields inserted
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #unescaped into a Redis command string (`setHash`). Test for Redis protocol injection via these
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #fields (e.g., embedding `\r\n` sequences or additional HSET arguments in `name`/`type`).
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `fs.folder` / `fs.file` — take a raw `path` string with no path-traversal or
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #allow-listing check visible (unlike the static GET handler, which explicitly rejects `..`).
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #Test:
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - `../../../../etc/passwd`, absolute paths (`/etc/shadow`), symlink traversal.
28bb29b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Confirm whether these RPC methods are reachable pre-authentication (they appear to require no
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #session token at all).
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `sys.write` / `sys.connect` — `sys.connect` spawns a real OS process via `vfork`+`execvp`
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #with a hardcoded binary path per current code, but confirm no code path allows the `name`/`guid`
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #parameters to influence the executable or arguments launched. `sys.write` forwards arbitrary bytes
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #to a connected process's stdin — test for terminal escape sequence injection (the JS client already
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #strips some ANSI codes defensively; verify server-side output isn't independently exploitable) and
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #for using this channel to pivot into shell command execution on any spawned interactive shell.
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `sys.setclock` — accepts attacker-controlled epoch millis and calls `settimeofday`. Test
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #authorization boundary (should require root — confirm process privilege level) and downstream
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #effects on TLS cert validation, log timestamps, and session-expiry logic elsewhere in the stack.
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- JSON parser fuzzing — `JSONParser::parseJSON` in json.h: test deeply nested
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #objects/arrays (stack exhaustion via `std::stack` growth), oversized numeric literals, malformed
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #`\u` escapes (currently a `TODO` — unescaped hex is not implemented, confirm it fails safely rather
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #than corrupting output), and control characters (checked for `<9` only — test `0x7F`–`0x9F` range
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #and multi-byte UTF-8 edge cases through the UTF-8→UTF-32 `convert32` conversion for exception
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #handling gaps).
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 4 — HTTP Layer Abuse
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Buffer/length handling — `HttpConnection::readBuffer` is a fixed 240,000-byte stack
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #buffer (`MaxRequest`). Test:
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Content-Length larger than buffer, negative/overflowed values via `longValue()` (uses `strtol`,
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #no bounds/error check) feeding the `while(n<contentLength)` read loop.
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #  - Truncated/slow-body requests (slow-loris style) against the 3-second `SO_RCVTIMEO` — confirm
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #the timeout actually terminates hung connections and doesn't leak the thread.
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Path traversal on static GET — verify the existing `path.find("..")` check can't be
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #bypassed via URL-encoding (`%2e%2e%2f`), double-encoding, or backslash variants, since `url_decode`
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #runs before the traversal check — confirm decode-then-check ordering is safe against
28bb29b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #encoded traversal sequences.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Header parsing — `onRequest()` builds an `Attributes` map from raw header lines with
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #minimal validation; test header injection (`\r\n` smuggling), duplicate headers, oversized header
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #blocks, and missing colon handling (`return false` observed — confirm this doesn't destabilize the
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #listener thread pool).
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Gzip content-type handling — automatic `.json`/`.raw` → `.gz` fallback path substitution:
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #test whether this can be leveraged to read a `.gz` file that shouldn't be transformed, or to serve
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #stale/incorrect `Content-Encoding`.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- 429/404/403 rate limiting — the current model uses blocking `usleep()` (9–12 seconds) on
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #suspected intruders inside the request-handling thread. Load-test with many concurrent
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #"intruder-triggering" requests to confirm this doesn't become a self-inflicted DoS (thread
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #pool exhaustion) rather than a mitigation.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 5 — Business Logic / Authorization Boundaries
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm `sys.shutdown` truly cannot be reached without `localconnection == true`, and confirm
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #nothing in the request path (headers like `Remote`, proxy trust) can be spoofed to flip that flag.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm there is no privilege distinction between a first-time anonymous visitor and any "admin"
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #concept — currently every RPC method appears equally reachable by any caller who can reach `/api`.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Document this explicitly as a finding if unintended.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- CSRF: `/api` accepts `POST` with `Content-Type: application/json` from any origin with no CSRF
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #token, and no `Origin`/`Referer` check visible. Test cross-site POST from a hosted third-party page
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #to confirm state-changing RPCs (`redis.put`, `sys.setclock`, `sys.connect`) can be triggered from a
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #victim's browser session against the target if reachable on a LAN/known hostname.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- CORS: confirm no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` is emitted — determine if that's relied upon as a
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #control, and test with `fetch()` cross-origin to verify actual browser enforcement versus intended
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #behavior.
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 6 — Secrets & Configuration
28bb29b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- `redis.h` contains a hardcoded Valkey password (`AUTH valkey2026`) compiled into the
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #binary/source. Flag as a finding regardless of network exposure — rotate and externalize via
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #environment/config, and audit git history for prior exposure.
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Review `CacheSalt`, `BlobSalt`, `ScanSalt`, `ConnectSalt`, `HandleSalt` in crypto.h — all are
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #static string literals in source. Since session tokens and handle keys derive from `sha512(name +
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #staticSalt)` with a low-entropy `name` (sequential counters), treat these as weak, enumerable
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #identifiers, not secure secrets. Recommend switching to a CSPRNG-derived session token instead
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #of hash-of-counter.
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm log file `StereoLog` (`../../cache/stereo.log`) doesn't world-write/world-read sensitive
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #data (RPC bodies, tokens) — `logLine` writes raw command/session content in several places
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #(`LOG_RPC`, `LOG_VALKEY` macros) — verify these debug macros are disabled in production
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #builds.
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 7 — Availability / DoS
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Thread-per-connection model (`pthread_create` per accepted socket, no pool/limit visible) — load
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #test with high concurrent connection counts to determine practical ceiling before resource
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #exhaustion (`HttpTaskCount` is tracked but not capped against a max).
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm oversized `redis.put` payloads (`MaxTransferSize` enforced client-side in JS only, at
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #15.9MB) are also bounded server-side — client-side limits are not a security control.
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Fuzz `sys.tick`'s `events` array size/content — verify unbounded event arrays from a single
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #session can't grow `EventSink::messages` without bound (no eviction/expiry visible in `EventSink`)
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #leading to unbounded memory growth over a long-running session.
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #Phase 8 — Client-Side (Web App) Review
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Audit `dsptool.js`/`dspacid32.js`/`dspsystem.js` terminal rendering paths for XSS via ANSI/log
28bb29ba [claude-sonnet-5] #content injected as text nodes (currently uses `createTextNode`, which is safe — confirm this
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #pattern is consistent everywhere logs/RPC replies are rendered, especially anywhere `innerHTML` is
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #used with server-derived strings, e.g., `wiki.writePage`'s markdown-to-HTML conversion).
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #- Specifically stress-test the wiki markdown renderer (`dspwiki.js` `writePage`) for
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #stored/reflected XSS — it builds `innerHTML` directly from converted markdown without visible
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #sanitization of raw HTML passthrough in fenced ` ```html ` blocks. Since wiki content is
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #stored/retrieved via `redis.run` `SET`/`GET` with no auth boundary noted, this is a plausible
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #stored XSS via wiki vector reachable by any RPC caller.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #- Confirm `KaTeX`'s `renderToString` is loaded with `throwOnError:false` safely and isn't a vector
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #for LaTeX-based DoS via pathological input.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #4. Priority Findings to Validate First
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #Ranked by likely impact based on this code review, confirm/deny each before broader testing:
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #1. `redis.run` exposed with no auth boundary — potential full backend compromise (data
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #loss, config tampering, Lua `EVAL` RCE within Redis).
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Wiki stored XSS via unsanitized markdown → `innerHTML`, compounded by unauthenticated
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #`SET wiki.*`.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #3. `fs.folder`/`fs.file` path traversal — no `..` guard, unlike the static-file GET path.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #4. Predictable session tokens derived from sequential counters + static salt.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #5. Hardcoded Redis credential in source.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #6. Plaintext HTTP only for an RPC surface that carries session tokens and file uploads.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #7. Sleep-based rate limiting causing thread exhaustion under concurrent abuse.
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bb [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #5. Tooling Suggestions
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #- `curl` / `httpie` for manual RPC probing.
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #- Burp Suite or `mitmproxy` for request tampering, session token analysis, CSRF PoC hosting.
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #- `redis-cli --no-auth-warning` against the proxied surface only (via `/api` `redis.run`),
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #not direct network access, unless separately authorized.
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #- Custom fuzzer (Python + `requests`) targeting the JSON-RPC `params` shapes per method — happy to
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #help write this harness if useful.
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #- `wrk`/`hey` for the thread-exhaustion and Content-Length abuse load tests.
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #6. Reporting Format
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #For each finding: description, affected file/function, reproduction steps, request/response
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #evidence, impact rating (CVSS or simple High/Med/Low), and remediation recommendation. Given
28bb29bc [claude-sonnet-5] #several findings above map directly to specific functions (`redisrun`, `jsonifyFSFolder`,
