28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #Connections to Earlier Discussion
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `dspwiki.js` — this almost certainly maps to the `wiki.banner` key we saw being
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #read/written in `stereo.log`. If you want, I can help trace how that Valkey key gets rendered into
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #the page.
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `wire_grid.js`, `wire_surface.js`, `wire_geometry.js`, `wire_topo.js` — these look like
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #strong candidates for whatever's consuming the `/aerialgrid/` endpoint and doing the pixel/canvas
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #work we discussed re: CORS and Web Workers. If the tainted-canvas issue is happening on this page,
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #these are probably where to look first.
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #A Few Things Worth Flagging
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #• 1. Avatar image has no `crossorigin` attribute:*
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #<img avatar alt="nitrologic" width="88px" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3953439"/>
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #Not an issue for normal display, but if this avatar is ever drawn onto a shared canvas (e.g., for a
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #user-icon overlay in the wire/grid view), it'll taint that canvas exactly like the earlier PNG
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #problem. Worth checking if any `wire_*.js` file touches this image.
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #• 2. 40+ synchronous `<script>` tags, no `defer`/`async`/modules:*
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #<script src="nitrojs/nitro-wire.js"></script>
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #<script src="nitrojs/spec-vsynth.js"></script>
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #...
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #This blocks rendering until every file loads sequentially. Not urgent, but if load time on this
28dd4de2 [claude-sonnet-5] #page is ever a concern, bundling or adding `defer` (assuming no inter-script execution-order
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #dependencies at parse time) would help.
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #• 3. Custom boolean-style attributes for styling:*
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #<div banner id="banner">
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #<div statusbar id="status"></div>
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #<img avatar ... />
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #Using bare attributes (`banner`, `statusbar`, `avatar`, `section`) instead of classes is a valid
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #but less common pattern — presumably targeted via `[banner]` CSS selectors in
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #`dsptool.css`/`wirepage.css`. Just flagging in case this was accidental rather than a deliberate
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #convention.
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #• 4. `theme-color` is red (`#FF0000`)* — probably intentional branding, but stands out next
28dd4de3 [claude-sonnet-5] #to `palette:night`, so wanted to confirm it's not a leftover/placeholder value.
