28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.363 514.7KB 17.91s
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Yes — `crossOrigin` is a standard DOM property, defined in the HTML Living Standard
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #(WHATWG), not something browser-specific or informal.
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Where It's Specified
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #It's part of the CORS settings attributes spec, which the WHATWG HTML spec defines here:
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #	ttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-settings-attributes
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #It applies to several elements beyond just `<img>`:
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `<img crossorigin>`
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `<script crossorigin>`
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `<link crossorigin>`
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `<video>` / `<audio>`
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `<use>` (SVG)
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Valid Values (Per Spec)
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #╭───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
28ddce11 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Value                │  Meaning                                                                 │
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #├───────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  `"anonymous"`        │  Send CORS request **without credentials** (no cookies)                  │
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  `"use-credentials"`  │  Send CORS request **with credentials** (cookies, HTTP auth)             │
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  *(missing/omitted)*  │  No CORS mode — regular request, canvas becomes tainted if cross-origin  │
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #╰───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #The "Invalid Value Default" Rule
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #This is the part that explains why `"dsptool"` in your code worked anyway. The spec defines
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #`crossOrigin` as an enumerated attribute with this exact rule:
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #	he invalid value default and missing value default are both the Anonymous
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #state.
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #So per spec: any string that isn't `"use-credentials"` — including typos, garbage strings,
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #or `"dsptool"` — is treated identically to `"anonymous"`. This isn't a browser quirk or fallback
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #hack; it's literally specified behavior, consistent across Chrome/Firefox/Safari.
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #Practical Takeaway
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = "anonymous";     // ✅ explicit, correct
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = "dsptool";       // ✅ works, but only by spec coincidence
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = "use-credentials"; // ⚠️ different mode, requires server ACAO to not be "*"
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = null;            // same as not setting it — no CORS mode at all
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #So your existing code isn't relying on undefined behavior — it's technically spec-compliant, just
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #misleading to read. Worth fixing for clarity, but not for correctness.
28ddce12 [claude-sonnet-5] #
