28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.379 517.3KB 21.32s
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #CORS as a concept predates Mr. Robot by several years.
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #Timeline
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #╭──────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Year    │  Milestone                                                │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #├──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  2009    │  W3C begins CORS Working Draft                            │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  2010    │  Firefox 3.5 adds early CORS support                      │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  2011    │  Chrome/WebKit implement `crossorigin` attribute on <img> │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  2014    │  CORS becomes official W3C Recommendation                 │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  2015    │  📺 Mr. Robot premieres (June 2015)                       │
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #╯──────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #So by the time Mr. Robot aired, `crossOrigin`/CORS had already been a finalized W3C standard for
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #about a year and a half, and browser support had existed for 3–4 years before that.
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #Why It Was Created
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f7 [claude-sonnet-5] #Worth noting the reason it exists ties into browser security history more broadly — CORS
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #was designed to relax the Same-Origin Policy (which itself dates back to Netscape Navigator
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #2.0 in 1995) in a controlled way, so that legitimate cross-origin requests (APIs, CDNs, fonts,
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #etc.) could happen safely without opening the door to the kind of data-exfiltration attacks
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Same-Origin Policy was originally meant to prevent.
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #So the timeline is roughly: 1995 Same-Origin Policy → 2009–2014 CORS spec development → 2015
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Mr. Robot. The mechanism you're using in `dsptool` today is essentially unchanged from what was
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #standardized a decade before the show existed.
28ddd0f8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
