28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #Got it — doing this manually through the Bunny CDN dashboard rather than the API. Here's
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #how to purge by tag from the web UI:
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #Steps to purge via Cache Tag in the Bunny CDN Dashboard
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Log in to your Bunny.net account.
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Go to your Pull Zone (the one serving `wiredjs/`).
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Open the Caching tab.
28de4d38 [claude-sonnet-5] #4. Look for the Cache Tags or Purge Cache section.
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #5. If you're purging by tag, there should be a field to enter the tag name (e.g.,
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #`wiredjs`) and a Purge button next to it.
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #6. Confirm the purge — Bunny will invalidate all cached objects associated with that tag across
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #edge nodes.
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #Important prerequisite
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #For tag-based purging to work, your origin server must already be sending the tag header on the
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #responses for files under `wiredjs/`, e.g.:
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #CDN-Cache-Tag: wiredjs
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #Without that header being set at origin (or via an Edge Rule), Bunny has nothing to purge by tag —
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #there'd be no files associated with `wiredjs`.
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you haven't set tags yet
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you just want to flush that folder right now without tags, you can also:
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Go to Caching → Purge Cache
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Enter the specific URL pattern (e.g., `https://yourzone.b-cdn.net/wiredjs/*`)
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Click Purge
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #That does an immediate wildcard purge without needing tags at all.
28de4d39 [claude-sonnet-5] #
