29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.037 20.53KB 9.88s
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #• Code - OSS is the open-source base of Visual Studio Code*.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Microsoft association
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- The source project is primarily developed by Microsoft and community contributors.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- It is published at [`microsoft/vscode`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode) under the MIT
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #licence.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Microsoft builds that source into the branded Visual Studio Code product, adding
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Microsoft branding, distribution terms, telemetry configuration, and access to Microsoft’s
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #extension marketplace.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Arch Linux’s `code` package is generally an independently compiled Code - OSS build
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #rather than Microsoft’s official binary.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Your version information therefore looks like an Arch-packaged build of the VS Code source.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #`ElectronBuildId: undefined` is usually only a packaging detail.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #The listed `@github/copilot` components indicate that Copilot support is installed or bundled in
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #that build. GitHub is owned by Microsoft, but its presence does not turn Code - OSS into the
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #official Microsoft VS Code distribution.
29060059 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #You can check which Arch package supplied it with:
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #pacman -Qo "$(command -v code)"
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #Typically:
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #- `code` — Arch’s Code - OSS build
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #- `visual-studio-code-bin` — Microsoft’s official branded build, commonly installed from the AUR
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #- `vscodium` — community build intended to remove Microsoft branding and telemetry defaults
2906005a [gpt-5.6-sol] #
