29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #• Code - OSS fork → shared branded product → platform-specific builds/installers*
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Shared application layer
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Maintain these once in your fork/build configuration:
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- `product.json` identity and application names
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Branding, icons and About information
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Extensions bundled with your product
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Developer-tool features
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Telemetry and privacy settings
29060b54 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Update-service configuration
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Extension registry, such as Open VSX
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Unique URL protocol and user-data directories
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Avoid putting core branding only in an Arch `PKGBUILD`, because it would then need to be recreated
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #for every operating system.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Platform-specific distribution
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #• Windows*
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Build x64 and, if needed, ARM64 versions.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Produce an `.exe` or MSI installer.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Use unique application IDs and installation directories.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Sign executables and installers with an Authenticode code-signing certificate.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Account for Windows Defender/SmartScreen reputation.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #• macOS*
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Build separate Apple Silicon and Intel versions, or a universal application.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Use your own reverse-domain bundle identifier.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Sign with an Apple Developer ID certificate.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Enable the appropriate hardened-runtime settings.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Notarize and staple the application.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Distribute as a signed `.dmg`, `.pkg`, or archive.
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #• Linux*
29060b55 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Provide packages such as Arch `PKGBUILD`, `.deb`, `.rpm`, AppImage or Flatpak.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Configure desktop entries, icons, MIME associations and protocol handlers.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Build infrastructure
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Use CI workers native to each target:
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Linux runner for Linux
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Windows runner for Windows
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- macOS runner for macOS
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Keep signing certificates and notarization credentials in protected CI secrets. Builds from
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #untrusted pull requests should never receive those secrets.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Important service and licensing points
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #The Code - OSS source is MIT-licensed, but Microsoft’s trademarks, artwork, marketplace access,
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #update infrastructure and proprietary extensions are separate. In particular:
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Use your own product name and visual identity.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Do not assume access to Microsoft’s Visual Studio Marketplace.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Consider Open VSX or your own extension registry.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Check redistribution terms for every bundled extension, including Copilot.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Retain applicable copyright and third-party notices.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #For a serious cross-platform product, the Arch package should be only one output of a common build
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #and release system—not the foundation of the product.
29060b56 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
