29198cef [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 9.174KB 7.18s
29198cef [gemini-3.8-flash] #For a standard Pull Zone, Bunny.net does not expose a metric for the total volume of data currently
29198cef [gemini-3.8-flash] #stored in the edge cache.
29198cef [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29198cef [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because the edge cache is distributed across global Points of Presence (POPs) on volatile NVMe/RAM
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #drives and operates on a Least Recently Used (LRU) eviction model, there is no single aggregate
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #"cache size" value.
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #However, the Bunny.net Statistics API does provide cache volume and efficiency metrics across given
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #time windows:
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Cached Bandwidth: The total volume of bytes served directly out of the edge cache without
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #hitting your origin.
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Origin Bandwidth: The volume of bytes fetched from `https://skid.nz` when cache misses
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #occur.
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Cache Hit Rate: The percentage of total requests satisfied by the cache versus those
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #forwarded to the origin.
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• (Note: If you were using a persistent Bunny Storage Zone rather than an external origin, the API
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #would report `StorageUsed` in bytes, but this does not apply to standard pull zones backed by a web
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #server).*
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you would like a script to pull the statistics report (including cached bandwidth and cache hit
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #rate) for zone `6621428`, please let me know.
29198cf0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919906d [skid@archlinux] will data last for days, weeks?
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.006 10.58KB 5.54s
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In practice, whether data remains cached for days or weeks depends on three primary factors:
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Your Origin's Cache Headers
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because your Cache Max-Age Override is set to `-1s`, Bunny.net adheres strictly to the
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #headers sent by `https://skid.nz`:
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• If your web server sends `Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000` (30 days), the edge nodes
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #consider the content fresh for up to 30 days.
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• If your origin sends short TTLs, `no-cache`, or omits expiration headers, files will expire
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #quickly or will not be cached at all.
291990d1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Request Frequency and LRU Eviction
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Even with a high `max-age`, edge servers use Least Recently Used (LRU) eviction:
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Each global Point of Presence (POP) has finite high-speed storage.
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• If an asset is not frequently requested through a specific POP, the edge server may evict it
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #after a few hours or days to free up capacity for higher-demand content.
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• High-traffic files stay cached for the full duration of their TTL.
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Per-POP Caching
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Each Bunny.net POP caches independently. A file requested by a visitor in Sydney is cached locally
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #in Sydney, but a subsequent visitor in London will trigger an origin fetch to populate the London
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #POP.
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Ensuring Multi-Week Retention
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you need assets to reliably stay cached for weeks regardless of request volume:
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Perma-Cache: Bunny.net offers a feature called Perma-Cache, which writes your
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #cached files to Bunny Storage nodes. This prevents LRU eviction on low-traffic files and serves all
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #POPs from the storage layer instead of querying your origin server.
291990d2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
