2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 14.57KB 31.17s
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #Based on this Nginx configuration, here is how long your data will last in the Bunny.net cache:
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. The Static Grid Locations (Will last weeks to months)
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #For paths such as `/aerialgrid/`, `/topogrid2/`, `/sd-aerialgrid/`, etc., your origin sends:
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable";
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Explicit Expiration: You are instructing Bunny.net that these files are valid for 1
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #year (`31,536,000` seconds) and will never change (`immutable`).
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Retention: Bunny.net will not expire these assets on its own schedule. They will persist
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #in the edge cache across days and weeks.
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• The Only Eviction Factor: If a specific regional POP receives very few requests for a
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #given tile or file, it may eventually be evicted via LRU (Least Recently Used) to free disk space
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #on that specific edge server. In high-traffic POPs (or if your user base is consistently active),
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #they will stay cached for the long term.
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. The Dynamic / Root Proxy (Will NOT last)
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #For requests falling through to `location /` (proxied to `localhost:8083`):
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• This block does not set any explicit `Cache-Control` header.
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Unless your backend process listening on `:8083` emits explicit caching headers, Bunny.net will
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #treat these responses as uncacheable or will cache them only for very short heuristic windows.
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960e [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #A Note on Your `add_header` Directives
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #In Nginx, the `add_header` directive does not inherit across blocks if child blocks define
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #their own `add_header`. Because you define `add_header Cache-Control` inside each `/...grid/`
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #location, the outer `Strict-Transport-Security` header is dropped for those specific
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #locations.
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you want HSTS sent on those static grid assets as well, you must duplicate that directive inside
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #each location block.
2919960f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199b85 [skid@archlinux] would 2 hours be ok for root?
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 16.61KB 3.28s
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Yes, 2 hours (`max-age=7200`) is often a very practical middle ground for dynamic
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #applications.
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Before implementing it, consider how your root application behaves:
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #When 2 Hours Works Well
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Semi-static assets: HTML shells, dynamic CSS bundles, scripts, or landing pages that
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #update periodically but not constantly.
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Database / Backend relief: It will shield your backend on `:8083` from repeated hits for
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #popular routes, serving those requests directly from the Bunny edge.
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Acceptable invalidation window: If you push a code update, you can either wait up to 2
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #hours for it to naturally propagate, or invoke your purge script (as in your first task) to force
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #an immediate refresh.
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #When 2 Hours Might Cause Issues
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Personalized / Session-based data: If responses differ per user (e.g., user profiles,
29199bc0 [gemini-3.8-flash] #login state, shopping carts, or set cookies), a public 2-hour cache will cause users to see each
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #other’s cached content.
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• State mutation APIs: POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints or dynamic JSON feeds that rely on
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #immediate consistency.
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Implementation Options
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you determine that your root endpoint is safe to cache publicly, you have two primary ways to
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #configure it:
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. At the Origin (Nginx):
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   Add the header directly inside `location /`:
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   location / {
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       proxy_pass http://backend;
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       proxy_http_version 1.1;
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       proxy_set_header Connection "keep-alive";
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       proxy_set_header X-Host $host;
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       proxy_set_header X-Remote $remote_addr;
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #       add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=7200";
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   }
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   (Alternatively, configure your backend application on `:8083` to emit this header).
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. At the CDN Level (Bunny.net Edge Rules):
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   If you want browser clients to revalidate more frequently than the CDN, you can configure
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #headers such as `Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=7200`. This instructs end-user
29199bc1 [gemini-3.8-flash] #browsers to cache for only 5 minutes, while Bunny.net keeps the edge copy fresh for 2 hours.
29199bc2 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
