2950f099 [skid@archlinux] how can i enable the digtopo code
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.011 426.2KB 18.99s
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #The `digTopo` path exists but is disabled at two points, and there's an ordering problem you'll hit
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #once you turn it on. Here's the full chain.
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #1. The feature switches
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #In `wire_graphics.js`, `Builder.buildTile` starts with a block of `const` flags. `digOutline` is
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #called from inside the `build_roof2` block:
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #const build_roof=false;
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #const build_roof2=false;         // <-- gate on the whole roof block
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #const build_roof_basement=true;  // <-- gate on digOutline inside it
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #Flip `build_roof2` to `true`. `build_roof_basement` is already `true`, so that's the only flag you
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #need. `build_roof` and `build_roof_geom`/`build_walls_geom` control separate features (scratch
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #drawing, wall geometry) — leave them off initially.
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #2. The ordering problem
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1ce [deepseek-flash] #`meshTile` in `wire_graphics.js` does this, in order:
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #tile.createScratch(AppPlatform.ScratchRes);
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #const surfaces = this.builder.buildTile(tile, 2);   // digOutline runs here
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #...
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #const topo = tile.topoSurface;                       // already built!
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #tile.tilemesh = layer0.addTileShape(topo, ...);
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #But `tile.topoSurface` was created earlier — either in `TopoTile.onBump` (worker path) or in
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #`GraphicsStack.bakeTileSurface` (no-baker path) — before `digOutline` mutated
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #`heightmap.ground`/`heightmap.diff`. So the dig will silently do nothing visible.
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #You need to rebuild the surface after `buildTile` returns. Add this to `meshTile`:
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #meshTile(tile, home){
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	this._activeTiles.push(tile);
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	const tx = (tile.x)*TileSize - home[0];
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	const ty = (tile.y)*TileSize - home[1];
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	const origin = [tx, ty, 0x4000];
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	const layer0 = this.view0.layer;
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	tile.createScratch(AppPlatform.ScratchRes);
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	const surfaces = this.builder.buildTile(tile, 2);
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1cf [deepseek-flash] #	// digTopo may have mutated heightmap.ground/diff; rebuild the surface
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	if(tile.heightmap){
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #		const topo = CreateTopoSurface(128, 16, GroundPen, tile.heightmap);
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #		const zfactor = 4.6/(tile.level*8.0);
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #		topo.calcNormals(zfactor);
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #		tile.topoSurface = topo;
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	}
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	tile.allocWallmap();
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	tile.staticmeesh = layer0.addStaticShapes(surfaces, tile.scratch, tile.wallmap, origin);
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	const topo = tile.topoSurface;
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #	tile.tilemesh = layer0.addTileShape(topo, tile.basemap, tile.scratch, origin);
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #}
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #`GroundPen` is declared in `wire_topo.js`, and the `zfactor` expression matches what
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #`TopoTile.onBump` uses — keep them consistent or the shading will differ between dug and undug
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #tiles.
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #3. Prerequisites
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #- `AppRuntime.UseLINZ` must be `true` (it is by default in `wire_grid.js`).
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #- The tile source must actually have a `roa` layer with `ROOF` outlines. That means the source
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #entry needs `"roaname" in layer` and `level < 3` in `fetchTopoTile`. The `ROOF` array in
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #`onDrawingResponse` will otherwise be empty and the whole `build_roof2` block is skipped by
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #`roofs.length`.
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #- `BasementDepth` in `wire_grid.js` is currently `4`. That's tiny — the dig will be nearly
2950f1d0 [deepseek-flash] #invisible. Bump it to something like `200` to test.
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #4. Debugging the bits
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #`Bits.digTopo` depends on `Bits.poly` producing a consistent even-odd scanline, and `poly` has two
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #rough edges that will bite on complex roofs:
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #- it only clamps `x`, not `y` (negative `y` silently drops writes on the typed array);
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #- it steps one pixel per Bresenham increment, so a thin diagonal can leave single-pixel gaps, and
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #`digTopo`'s `on = !on` toggling then inverts the wrong region.
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #Before wiring it up, call `bits.dump()` on a known roof outline to see the filled region as `X`/`.`
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #ASCII. If the fill looks correct in the dump, `digTopo` will behave. If it looks like a stipple
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #pattern instead of a solid interior, the `poly` fill is the thing to fix, not `digTopo`.
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #5. What `digTopo` actually writes
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #For reference, so you can verify the effect is reaching the surface:
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #heightmap.setGround(tx+bx, ty+by, depth);  // pickGround returns this when nonzero
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #heightmap.setHeight(tx+bx, ty+by, 0);      // clears diff (detail height)
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #`CreateTopoSurface` reads `pickTopo(...).ground` and uses `const z = ground || minz;` — so a
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #nonzero `ground` overrides the terrain elevation and the vertex drops to the basement depth. The
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #`border` argument (40 in the call site) is a halo in heightmap pixels, not world units —
2950f1d1 [deepseek-flash] #worth tuning once you can see it working.
2950f1d2 [deepseek-flash] #
2950f1d2 [deepseek-flash] #Start with `BasementDepth = 200`, `build_roof2 = true`, and the `meshTile` rebuild in place. If
2950f1d2 [deepseek-flash] #nothing appears, dump `bits` first.
2950f1d2 [deepseek-flash] #
