297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #That is the only main-thread addition, and it is pure data marshalling — no geometry, no
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #rasterising, no surface building.
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #Remove the main-thread dig
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #`Builder.buildTile`'s `build_roof2` block currently calls `tile.digOutline`. With the dig moved to
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #the worker it must not run again — the worker already zeroed `diff` and set `ground` before the
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #buffers were transferred. Delete that call (or the whole `build_roof2` block if you weren't using
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #the rest of it). Leaving it in would dig a second time on an already-transferred heightmap, which
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #is at best a no-op and at worst double-offsets `ground`.
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #Ordering guarantees
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #- The worker's two gates (`topoCount` and `digReady`) mean `createTopo` fires only when both the
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #merged heightmap and the outlines are present, regardless of which arrived first.
297b6c65 [deepseek-flash] #- `postFlora` reads `diff`, which `digTopo` has already zeroed over each footprint, so building
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #cells fail `m.min>floraMin` and are omitted from the flora grid.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #- `post` transfers `topo`/`diff`/`ground` after both the dig and the flora pass, so the main thread
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #receives a single, final, consistent state — no rebuild in `meshTile`, no second flora pass, no
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #ordering assumptions on the main side.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #Small things
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #- `BasementDepth` is `4` in `wire_grid.js`. At that value the dig is invisible against the terrain.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #Bump it before you can judge the result — a few hundred is a reasonable starting point.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #- `Bits.poly` clamps `x` but not `y`; a negative `y` writes off the typed array. Roof outlines near
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #the tile edge will hit this. Worth fixing in `wire_util.js` before the worker starts relying on it.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #- `FloraPen` is `32`, which is outside `RoaPalette`'s 0–29 range. Set it to a real green (4, 9, 15,
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #24) — otherwise the flora you're now correctly generating will still render as whatever the driver
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #returns for an out-of-bounds uniform read.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #- `postFlora` writes `0,0,0` normals. `TopoFloraSurface` in `wire_core.js` does the same. Whichever
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #side ends up generating flora, `calcNormals` has to run on it before upload, or the surface stays
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #flat-lit regardless of the palette fix.
297b6c66 [deepseek-flash] #
