29853daf [deepseek-flash] #Two items I want to flag now because they change the shape of the sprint:
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #- `importScripts` side effects. `wire_util.js` runs `const AppEventServer=new
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #EventServer();` at top level, and `EventServer`'s constructor does `new Worker(...)`. Importing the
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #whole file into the baker will attempt a nested worker with a bad relative path. Either guard that
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #one line or carve out a small `wire_dig.js`. The doc recommends guarding.
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #- `BasementDepth=4` is not a bug, it's a unit problem. `SeaLevel=186*16` implies the
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #heightmap works in 1/16 m steps, so `4` ≈ 25 cm. The knob needs a value in those units, not a
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #different algorithm.
29853daf [deepseek-flash] #
