29853daf [roha] # Sprint Design — Dig House Footprints (Flora Exclusion)
29853daf [roha] **Status:** draft for review
29853daf [roha] **Scope:** `worker_baker.js`, `wire_util.js`, `wire_topo.js`, `wire_graphics.js`, `wire_grid.js`
29853daf [roha] **Owner:** Simon Armstrong
29853daf [roha] **Depends on:** tools enabled this sprint
29853daf [roha] ---
29853daf [roha] ## Review checklist (for this document)
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Goal and non-goals agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Current pipeline described accurately
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Reason the dig must run in the worker is stated and accepted
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Rejected alternatives recorded (main-thread rebuild)
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Extraction of a shared `digOutline` agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Worker protocol (`dig`) agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Worker gate (`topoCount` + `digReady`) agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] `createTopo` ordering (dig → `postFlora` → `post`) agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Main-thread marshalling agreed (no geometry on main)
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Removal of the main-thread dig agreed
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Prerequisites listed with owners
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Test plan sufficient
29853daf [roha] - [ ] Acceptance criteria testable
29853daf [roha] ---
29853daf [roha] ## 1. Goal
29853daf [roha] Dig building footprints (`ROOF` outlines from the LINZ `roagrid` drawings) into the
29853daf [roha] tile heightmap **before** the flora surface is generated, so that:
29853daf [roha] 1. Scrub/tree cells that fall on a house footprint are excluded from the flora grid.
29853daf [roha] 2. The basement depression is baked into the terrain surface in the same pass.
29853daf [roha] ## 2. Non-goals
29853daf [roha] - Not building roof or wall geometry. `build_roof_geom` and `build_walls_geom` stay off.
29853daf [roha] - Not changing the roof scratch drawing or `build_roof2`'s scratch overlay.
29853daf [roha] - Not supporting the no-baker path (`hasBaker=false`) this sprint. It is debug-only.
29853daf [roha] ## 3. Current pipeline
29853daf [roha] The worker merges the raw topo tiles, builds flora, then posts the bumpmap:
29853daf [roha] ```js
29853daf [roha] // worker_baker.js — createTopo()
29853daf [roha] function createTopo(){
29853daf [roha] 	const bytes=heightmaps[0]||[];
29853daf [roha] 	const heightmap=AllocBumpmap(bytes);
29853daf [roha] 	heightmap.setBytes(bytes);
29853daf [roha] 	const n=heightmaps.length;
29853daf [roha] 	for(let i=1;i<n;i++){
29853daf [roha] 		if(heightmaps[i].length==bytes.length){
29853daf [roha] 			heightmap.orBytes(heightmaps[i]);
29853daf [roha] 		}
29853daf [roha] 	}
29853daf [roha] 	heightmap.postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22);	// flora built from diff, pre-dig
29853daf [roha] 	heightmap.post();
29853daf [roha] 	heightmaps.length=0;
29853daf [roha] }
29853daf [roha] ```
29853daf [roha] `post()` transfers the buffers, which detaches them in the worker:
29853daf [roha] ```js
29853daf [roha] // worker_baker.js — Bumpmap.post()
29853daf [roha] post(){
29853daf [roha] 	const topo=this.topo;
29853daf [roha] 	const diff=this.diff;
29853daf [roha] 	const ground=this.ground;
29853daf [roha] 	const message=[{command:"bump",topo,diff,ground}];
29853daf [roha] 	const transfer=[topo.buffer,diff.buffer,ground.buffer];
29853daf [roha] 	postMessage(message,transfer);
29853daf [roha] }
29853daf [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] The only existing dig lives on `TopoTile`, runs on the main thread, and is gated off:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_graphics.js — Builder.buildTile()
29853db0 [roha] const build_roof2=false;
29853db0 [roha] ...
29853db0 [roha] if(build_roof2 && roofs.length){
29853db0 [roha] 	...
29853db0 [roha] 	if(build_roof_basement){
29853db0 [roha] 		tile.digOutline(outline,BasementDepth,40);
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	...
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] `Bits.digTopo` is the routine that performs the actual carve:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_util.js — Bits.digTopo()
29853db0 [roha] heightmap.setGround(tx+bx,ty+by,depth);
29853db0 [roha] heightmap.setHeight(tx+bx,ty+by,0);	// diff zeroed over the footprint
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ## 4. Problem
29853db0 [roha] Two facts force the design:
29853db0 [roha] 1. **Flora is built before any outline is known.** `postFlora` reads `diff`; nothing
29853db0 [roha]    has zeroed `diff` over the footprints yet.
29853db0 [roha] 2. **The dig cannot be applied after `post()`.** The typed arrays are detached by the
29853db0 [roha]    transfer, so there is nothing left to dig into on either side.
29853db0 [roha] Therefore the dig must run **inside the worker**, before `postFlora` and before `post`.
29853db0 [roha] ## 5. Design decision: worker-first
29853db0 [roha] The worker owns dig, flora and post. The main thread's only new responsibility is to
29853db0 [roha] forward the roof outlines once they have been parsed.
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] main                                worker
29853db0 [roha] ────                                ──────
29853db0 [roha] fetchTileRaw ────heightmap────────▶ accumulate
29853db0 [roha] fetchDrawing                        (hold; do not post)
29853db0 [roha]   onDrawingResponse
29853db0 [roha]     extract ROOF outlines
29853db0 [roha]     maybeSendDig ───dig────────────▶ store outlines, digReady=true
29853db0 [roha]                                      refresh(): topoCount && digReady ?
29853db0 [roha]                                        dig each outline
29853db0 [roha]                                        postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22)
29853db0 [roha]                                        post() ──────▶ main
29853db0 [roha]                                      (buffers transferred here)
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ### Rejected alternative — rebuild flora on the main thread
29853db0 [roha] Generate flora in `meshTile` after `buildTile` returns, overwriting the worker's
29853db0 [roha] `floraSurface`. Rejected because:
29853db0 [roha] - Two flora passes per tile (worker's is discarded).
29853db0 [roha] - Ordering becomes implicit — the dig's effect depends on `buildTile` having run.
29853db0 [roha] - It puts surface construction on the main thread, against the existing shape where
29853db0 [roha]   the worker owns all heightmap-derived surfaces.
29853db0 [roha] The rebuild remains available as a five-line fallback if the worker path stalls.
29853db0 [roha] ## 6. Shared geometry
29853db0 [roha] `TopoTile.digOutline` only reads `Bits` and a heightmap — no tile state — so it can be
29853db0 [roha] hoisted to a free function in `wire_util.js` and used by both sides.
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_util.js — new free function
29853db0 [roha] function digOutline(heightmap,outline,deep,border){
29853db0 [roha] 	let xmin=1e9;
29853db0 [roha] 	let xmax=-1e9;
29853db0 [roha] 	let ymin=1e9;
29853db0 [roha] 	let ymax=-1e9;
29853db0 [roha] 	let zmin=1e9;
29853db0 [roha] 	const pts=[];
29853db0 [roha] 	const n=outline.length;
29853db0 [roha] 	for(let w=0;w<n;w++){
29853db0 [roha] 		const o=outline[w];
29853db0 [roha] 		const x=(o[0]/2)|0;
29853db0 [roha] 		const y=(o[1]/2)|0;
29853db0 [roha] 		const h0=heightmap.pickTopo(x,y).min;
29853db0 [roha] 		zmin=Math.min(zmin,h0);
29853db0 [roha] 		if(x<xmin) xmin=x;
29853db0 [roha] 		if(x>xmax) xmax=x;
29853db0 [roha] 		if(y<ymin) ymin=y;
29853db0 [roha] 		if(y>ymax) ymax=y;
29853db0 [roha] 		pts.push([x,y]);
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	const width=(xmax-xmin)|0;
29853db0 [roha] 	const height=(ymax-ymin)|0;
29853db0 [roha] 	const depth=(zmin-deep)|0;
29853db0 [roha] 	const bits=new Bits(width,height,xmin,ymin);
29853db0 [roha] 	bits.poly(pts);
29853db0 [roha] 	bits.digTopo(heightmap,depth,border);
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] Coordinates are halved because the drawing space is 4096 and the heightmap space is
29853db0 [roha] 2048 (`scale=TileSize/4096.0` in `drawOutline`). `Bits` is allocated with `xmin,ymin`
29853db0 [roha] as its origin, so `poly`'s inputs are non-negative by construction.
29853db0 [roha] `TopoTile.digOutline` is deleted once this lands.
29853db0 [roha] ## 7. Worker protocol
29853db0 [roha] One new command. Outlines are plain arrays (structured-clone, no transfer list).
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] {command:"dig", outlines:[...], depth:BasementDepth, border:BasementBorder}
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] `depth` and `border` are sent from the main thread so the tuning knobs stay next to
29853db0 [roha] `BasementDepth` in `wire_grid.js`:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_grid.js
29853db0 [roha] const BasementDepth=4;		// TODO: units are 1/16 m — see §10
29853db0 [roha] const BasementBorder=40;	// halo in heightmap pixels
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ## 8. Worker gate
29853db0 [roha] The worker must not build until it has both the merged heightmap and the outlines.
29853db0 [roha] Two independent gates, so arrival order does not matter.
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // worker_baker.js — top of file
29853db0 [roha] importScripts("../wirejs/wire_util.js");	// Bits + digOutline
29853db0 [roha] let topoCount;
29853db0 [roha] let digReady=false;
29853db0 [roha] let digDepth=4;
29853db0 [roha] let digBorder=40;
29853db0 [roha] const heightmaps=[];
29853db0 [roha] const roofOutlines=[];
29853db0 [roha] function refresh(){
29853db0 [roha] 	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady){
29853db0 [roha] 		createTopo();
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] Command dispatch gains one case:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] case "dig":
29853db0 [roha] 	onDig(line.outlines,line.depth,line.border);
29853db0 [roha] 	break;
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] function onDig(outlines,depth,border){
29853db0 [roha] 	for(const o of outlines){
29853db0 [roha] 		roofOutlines.push(o);
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	digDepth=depth;
29853db0 [roha] 	digBorder=border;
29853db0 [roha] 	digReady=true;
29853db0 [roha] 	refresh();
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] `refresh()` is already called from `onHeightmap` and `onTopoCount`; `onDig` adds the
29853db0 [roha] third call site.
29853db0 [roha] ## 9. `createTopo` ordering
29853db0 [roha] The dig sits between the merge and the flora pass. This is the whole sprint.
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] function createTopo(){
29853db0 [roha] 	const bytes=heightmaps[0]||[];
29853db0 [roha] 	const heightmap=AllocBumpmap(bytes);
29853db0 [roha] 	heightmap.setBytes(bytes);
29853db0 [roha] 	const n=heightmaps.length;
29853db0 [roha] 	for(let i=1;i<n;i++){
29853db0 [roha] 		if(heightmaps[i].length==bytes.length){
29853db0 [roha] 			heightmap.orBytes(heightmaps[i]);
29853db0 [roha] 		}
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	heightmaps.length=0;
29853db0 [roha] 	// footprints dug before flora samples diff
29853db0 [roha] 	for(const outline of roofOutlines){
29853db0 [roha] 		digOutline(heightmap,outline,digDepth,digBorder);
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	roofOutlines.length=0;
29853db0 [roha] 	heightmap.postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22);
29853db0 [roha] 	heightmap.post();
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] Because `digTopo` writes `diff=0` over each footprint, the flora test
29853db0 [roha] `m.min>floraMin` (with `floraMin=22`) fails on those cells and they are omitted.
29853db0 [roha] Flora and bump remain two separate messages. `TileInstance.onMessage` and
29853db0 [roha] `hasLoaded()` are unchanged, which keeps the diff small.
29853db0 [roha] ## 10. Main-thread marshalling
29853db0 [roha] The only new main-thread code. It collects `ROOF` outlines from every drawing and
29853db0 [roha] sends one `dig` message once all drawings have landed — including the zero-drawings
29853db0 [roha] case, or the worker gate would never open.
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_topo.js — TopoTile constructor
29853db0 [roha] this.digSent=false;
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_topo.js — new method
29853db0 [roha] maybeSendDig(){
29853db0 [roha] 	if(this.digSent) return;
29853db0 [roha] 	if(this.drawingCount!=this.drawings.length) return;
29853db0 [roha] 	this.digSent=true;
29853db0 [roha] 	const outlines=[];
29853db0 [roha] 	for(const d of this.drawings){
29853db0 [roha] 		for(const roof of d.data["ROOF"]){
29853db0 [roha] 			const start=roof.start;
29853db0 [roha] 			const count=roof.count;
29853db0 [roha] 			for(let i=0;i<count;i++){
29853db0 [roha] 				outlines.push(d.outlines[start+i]);
29853db0 [roha] 			}
29853db0 [roha] 		}
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] 	if(this.instance){
29853db0 [roha] 		this.instance.post([{
29853db0 [roha] 			command:"dig",
29853db0 [roha] 			outlines,
29853db0 [roha] 			depth:BasementDepth,
29853db0 [roha] 			border:BasementBorder
29853db0 [roha] 		}]);
29853db0 [roha] 	}
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] Called from two places:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_topo.js — end of onDrawingResponse()
29853db0 [roha] this.drawings.push(drawing);
29853db0 [roha] this.dirty=true;
29853db0 [roha] this.maybeSendDig();
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_topo.js — end of fetchTopoTile(), after the source loop
29853db0 [roha] this.maybeSendDig();
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] The second call covers levels where no `roaname` is fetched (`level>=3`) and
29853db0 [roha] `UseLINZ=false`, sending an empty outline list so `digReady` becomes true.
29853db0 [roha] ## 11. Removal of the main-thread dig
29853db0 [roha] Digging is now the worker's job. Remove the call so a future `build_roof2=true` does
29853db0 [roha] not double-dig an already-transferred heightmap:
29853db0 [roha] ```js
29853db0 [roha] // wire_graphics.js — Builder.buildTile(), build_roof2 block
29853db0 [roha] if(build_roof_basement){
29853db0 [roha] 	tile.digOutline(outline,BasementDepth,40);	// DELETE
29853db0 [roha] }
29853db0 [roha] ```
29853db0 [roha] ## 12. Prerequisites
29853db0 [roha] | Item | Detail | Owner |
29853db0 [roha] |------|--------|-------|
29853db0 [roha] | `importScripts` side effects | `wire_util.js` runs `const AppEventServer=new EventServer();` at top level and `EventServer` constructs a `Worker`. Guard it: `const AppEventServer=(typeof window!=="undefined")?new EventServer():null;` | — |
29853db0 [roha] | `importScripts` path | Worker URL is `.../nitrojs/worker_baker.js`, so the path is `"../wirejs/wire_util.js"`. Verify in devtools. | — |
29853db0 [roha] | `BasementDepth` units | `SeaLevel=186*16` implies 16 steps per metre, so `4` ≈ 25 cm. Choose a visible depth in those units. | — |
29853db0 [roha] | `FloraPen` | Now `20` (mint, alpha 0.52). In range for `RoaPalette` (0–29). | done |
29853db0 [roha] | Flora normals | `postFlora` writes `0,0,0` normals and `addTileShape` does not call `calcNormals`. Flora stays flat-lit regardless of palette. Fix in `TopoTile.onFlora`: `this.floraSurface.calcNormals(4.6/(this.level*8.0));` | — |
29853db0 [roha] | `Bits.poly` bounds | The `y` clamp is commented out and the width computation may drop the final row/column. Harmless for typed arrays (writes ignored) but can drop edge parity. Validate with `bits.dump()`. | — |
29853db0 [roha] ## 13. Test plan
29853db0 [roha] 1. **Bits rasterisation.** For a known roof outline, call `outlinePoints`-style setup and
29853db0 [roha]    `bits.dump()`. Expect a solid `X` interior, not a stipple. Fix `poly` before judging
29853db0 [roha]    the dig.
29853db0 [roha] 2. **Single tile, one roof.** Load level 1 over a known house. Confirm the basement
29853db0 [roha]    appears and flora is absent over the footprint.
29853db0 [roha] 3. **Depth sweep.** Render at `BasementDepth` 4, 16, 64, 256. Pick the smallest value
29853db0 [roha]    that reads as a footprint.
29853db0 [roha] 4. **Edge outline.** Find a roof crossing a tile boundary. Confirm no dropped parity and
29853db0 [roha]    no spurious dig outside the footprint.
29853db0 [roha] 5. **Zero-outline level.** Load `level>=3`. Confirm the tile still loads (empty `dig`).
29853db0 [roha] 6. **Drawings-before-topo.** Throttle the topo fetch; confirm the gate still fires once.
29853db0 [roha] ## 14. Risks
29853db0 [roha] | Risk | Mitigation |
29853db0 [roha] |------|-----------|
29853db0 [roha] | Fetch-error path never calls `onDrawingResponse`, so `drawingCount` never settles | Pre-existing; `hasLoaded()` fails the same way. Log and out of scope. |
29853db0 [roha] | `Bits.poly` parity drop on thin diagonal edges | `bits.dump()` test; clip or clamp if needed. |
29853db0 [roha] | `importScripts` pulls browser-only top-level code into the worker | Guard `AppEventServer`; audit `wire_util.js` top level. |
29853db0 [roha] | No-baker path (`hasBaker=false`) has no worker to dig | Out of scope; document as unsupported. |
29853db0 [roha] | Roof outlines split across tiles | Each tile digs the outlines it fetched; overlap is idempotent (`setGround`/`setHeight` are writes). |
29853db0 [roha] ## 15. Acceptance criteria
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] `wire_util.js` guarded so it imports cleanly into the baker.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] `digOutline` is a free function; `TopoTile.digOutline` removed.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Worker handles `dig`, gates on `topoCount && digReady`.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] `createTopo` digs, then `postFlora`, then `post`.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] `maybeSendDig` called from `onDrawingResponse` and `fetchTopoTile`.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Main-thread `tile.digOutline` call removed.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Flora absent over footprints at level 1.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Basement visible at the chosen `BasementDepth`.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Tile loads at `level>=3` with zero outlines.
29853db0 [roha] - [ ] Flora lit (not flat-dark) after the `calcNormals` fix.
29853db0 [roha] ## 16. Open questions
29853db0 [roha] 1. Should the dig also suppress the `ROOF` scratch drawing, or does the basement fill
29853db0 [roha]    already cover it?
29853db0 [roha] 2. Should flora exclusion use a larger `border` than the basement carve, so trees clear
29853db0 [roha]    the eaves rather than the wall line?
29853db0 [roha] 3. Do we want the depth to come from the drawing attributes (storey count) rather than a
29853db0 [roha]    single global `BasementDepth`?
