29859a63 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.024 905.2KB 46.61s
29859a63 [deepseek-flash] #Yes — there's a distinction, but it's derived rather than stored, and one half of it leaks. That
29859a63 [deepseek-flash] #matters because a stats report built on the leaky half will show a number that only ever grows.
29859a63 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a63 [deepseek-flash] #What "active" currently means
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #Three separate notions exist, and they aren't the same set:
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #╭───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #│  Notion       │  Where                                      │  Meaning                                                                                                       │
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #│  **Touched**  │  `TopoTile.frame` vs `TopoGrid.frameCount`  │  Set by `touchTiles` for tiles that are `fetched && ready`; `sweep` removes them once `frame < frameCount-20`  │
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #│  **Meshed**   │  `GraphicsStack._activeTiles`               │  Pushed in `meshTile`; never removed                                                                           │
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #│  **Cached**   │  `TopoGrid._tileGrid`                       │  Everything in the grid, whether touched or not                                                                │
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #╰───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #So "active vs cached" is `tile.frame >= frameCount-20` versus the rest of `_tileGrid`. That's
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #computable. But two things are broken around it:
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #- `GraphicsStack.flushTile` never splices `_activeTiles`. It removes the meshes from the
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #layers and calls `tile.retire()`, but the tile stays in the array. That array grows for the
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #lifetime of the session, so `_activeTiles.length` is a leak counter, not an active count.
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #- `sweep` skips tiles whose `frame` was never set. The guard is `if(tile.frame &&
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #tile.frame<minFrame)`, and `undefined` is falsy, so a tile that was created by `tileGet` but never
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #touched — a failed load, or one created via `TopoGrid.pick` — is never swept and is retained
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #forever. Those are the real "cached" population.
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #Both are worth fixing before the number means anything.
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #Memory: what's reachable
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #The dominant cost is the heightmap, and it's fully reachable: `Bumpmap.topo/diff/ground` are
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #`Uint16Array(resres)`, so `3  res² * 2` bytes per tile. At `res=1024` that's 6.3 MB per
29859a64 [deepseek-flash] #tile; a radius-5 view holds ~81 tiles, so ~500 MB. That dwarfs everything else.
29859a65 [deepseek-flash] #
29859a65 [deepseek-flash] #Surfaces and shapes are reachable too, except GPU buffer sizes, which are computed in
29859a65 [deepseek-flash] #`Shape.staticBuffer`/`instanceBuffer` and then discarded. Textures are counted in `SharedTextures`
29859a65 [deepseek-flash] #but without dimensions. Both need a little bookkeeping to report honestly.
