298700d1 [kimi-k3] #Here's where we've been and where we are.
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #The project
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #`wirejs` — a WebGL2 isometric tile renderer for NZ map data (LINZ aerial/topo/roa via
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #`grid7.b-cdn.net`), with a per-tile baker worker that merges raw heightmaps into a `Bumpmap`
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #(topo/diff/ground), builds flora and terrain surfaces, and posts them back to the main thread.
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #Threads of work, in order
298700d1 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #• 1. Flora darkness.* Diagnosed as two causes: zero normals (`postFlora` writes `0,0,0` and
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #nothing calls `calcNormals`) and `FloraPen` out of palette range (32, 31 — palette is 0–29). You
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #settled on hardcoded `15` in `postFlora(512,4,15,2)`. The `calcNormals` fix in `onFlora` is still
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #outstanding.
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #• 2. Dig footprints for houses.* The long design arc:
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #- My first answer was main-thread rebuild after `buildTile` — you pushed back: "worker role
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #must come first."
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #- Final design: main thread forwards ROOF outlines in a `dig` message; worker gates on `topoCount
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #&& digReady`, then digs → `postFlora` → `post`, so flora and terrain are built from already-dug
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #state.
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #- I wrote a design doc (submitted as `submission-6ab98dd7.md`) covering the gate, `maybeSendDig`,
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #`importScripts` hazards, and prerequisites.
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #• 3. LogStats.* You asked for tile cache + memory stats. My full design was rejected as
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #crud; you wanted ≤20 lines in your style. Shipped `totalTiles` (heightmap bytes), then merged
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #aerial pixel bytes into the same function. Confirmed working — 9 MB logged.
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #• 4. Baker dig implementation.* From the latest files: you've implemented it yourself —
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #`digReady` gate, `onDig`, dig loop in `createTopo`, `case "dig"` in the worker dispatch, and a
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #`dig` stub in `TopoProcess.onMessage`. Not yet visible: `maybeSendDig` on the main thread, which is
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #what actually sends outlines to the worker.
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #Current open issue
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #• Draw order of tiles.* Draw order == mesh order == load-completion order (nearest first,
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #so front-to-back). I asked which symptom you're seeing before writing the fix:
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #
298700d2 [kimi-k3] #- Seams between tiles → terrain alpha `O=0.94` forcing blend; make it opaque.
298700d3 [kimi-k3] #- Far tile painting over near → depth/culling problem, not order.
298700d3 [kimi-k3] #- Flora blending wrong when panning → needs back-to-front sort in the draw path, not at mesh time.
298700d3 [kimi-k3] #
298700d3 [kimi-k3] #Carried-over loose ends
