29a237cf [deepseek-flash] #- Nothing calls it.
29a237cf [deepseek-flash] #
29a237cf [deepseek-flash] #It's the right shape, just needs the extraction loop and a call site. Or delete it until you're
29a237cf [deepseek-flash] #ready.
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #`wire_graphics.js` — walls on, with two behaviour changes
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #`build_walls_geom=true` now generates wall geometry, which is a new feature live. Alongside it,
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #`walledSpiral` changed:
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #// base ring
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #const g0=topo.pickElevation(px,py);   // was pickGround
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #verts.push([px,-py,g0,pu,0,0,0,wallc]);
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #// top ring
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #const h1=+1600;                        // was topo.sampleHeight(px,py,2).max
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #verts.push([px,-py,h0+h1,pu,0,0,0,wallc]);
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #Two consequences:
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #- Base no longer follows the dig. `pickGround` returns the dug depth when `ground[i]` is
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #set; `pickElevation` ignores it. So walls sit at terrain level and the basement carves below them —
29a237d0 [deepseek-flash] #which is probably what you want, but it does mean walls and basement are now decoupled.
