29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.020 1.650MB 4.42s
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #Glad that landed — the `/4096` vs `/2048` split was a sneaky one to spot from behaviour alone.
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #Two things worth remembering while it's fresh:
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #- `rayVertex` has no divisor at all, so `pointLayer` (tagged both passes) sits at NDC z ≈ 0.5 in
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #the depth-enabled pass. Lines are `depthDisable` so they're fine, but points will be occluded by
29a30fa5 [deepseek-flash] #anything in front. If you use them for picking or markers, they'll need the same `/2048`.
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #- `zbias` is now your lever if seams come back at grazing angles — one constant per shader, and
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #terrain/walls/tiles are all in the same NDC space now, so it'll behave predictably.
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #And the earlier `BasementDepth=4` (~25 cm) is still worth a bump now that the dig can actually be
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #seen — you'll get much clearer feedback while tuning.
29a30fa6 [deepseek-flash] #
